description: An open civic-technology community in Japan building tools for public listening, deliberation, transparency, and policy feedback.
metas:
  lang: en
---
<div>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-xl my-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold">
      <span class="box-decoration-clone gradient inline py-1">
        Digital Democracy 2030
      </span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-relaxed">
      Building democratic infrastructure so more voices can be heard, organized,
      and reflected in public decision-making.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="#projects" class="btn btn-primary">
        Explore the projects →
      </a>
      <a href="/join-us" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-primary">
        Join / contact (Japanese) →
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/digitaldemocracy2030"
        class="btn btn-outline"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        GitHub →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-xl mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-3xl">What DD2030 is</h2>
    <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
      Digital Democracy 2030, or DD2030, is an open civic-technology community
      in Japan. We use AI and digital tools to support public listening,
      deliberation, transparency, and policy feedback.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
      DD2030 is not a single centrally controlled organization. It is a loose,
      participatory community where people contribute as developers,
      researchers, designers, organizers, policymakers, and citizens.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-xl mt-20">
    <div class="gradient w-full h-0.5"></div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl mt-5">Political neutrality</h2>
    <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
      DD2030 does not support or oppose any political party, candidate, or
      political organization. Its neutrality means both party neutrality and
      procedural neutrality: the same rules and conditions should apply to
      everyone.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
      DD2030&apos;s tools may be used by municipalities, parties, civic groups,
      researchers, companies, or other organizations under the same rules. Use
      of a tool does not imply DD2030 endorsement.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/about/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-outline">
        About DD2030 (Japanese) →
      </a>
      <a href="/contribution/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-outline">
        Contributor guidelines (Japanese) →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" class="mx-auto max-w-xl mt-20">
    <div class="gradient w-full h-0.5"></div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl mt-5">Projects</h2>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <hgroup class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <div class="gradient w-1"></div>
        <div class="w-[calc(100%-12px)]">
          <h3 class="text-2xl">Broad Listening</h3>
          <p class="font-bold mt-2">
            Collecting diverse voices and making them easier to understand.
          </p>
        </div>
      </hgroup>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Broad listening is a practice for gathering many perspectives,
        organizing them, and making the structure of public opinion easier to
        inspect. DD2030 also supports a book project that explains the concept,
        cases, and implementation methods.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/broad-listening/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-primary">
          Learn more (Japanese) →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://broadlisteningbook.com/en/"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Book site →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <hgroup class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <div class="gradient w-1"></div>
        <div class="w-[calc(100%-12px)]">
          <h3 class="text-2xl">Kouchou AI</h3>
          <p class="font-bold mt-2">
            Open-source analysis software for broad listening.
          </p>
        </div>
      </hgroup>
      <img
        src="/en/images/kouchou-ai-broad-listening.webp"
        width="1862"
        height="845"
        alt="Kouchou AI interface image"
        class="w-full mt-4"
      />
      <p class="mt-4">
        Kouchou AI builds on ideas from Talk to the City and adapts them for
        practical use by Japanese municipalities, political actors, and other
        organizations. It helps analyze large sets of comments while keeping
        human judgment central.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/kouchou-ai/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-primary">
          Learn more (Japanese) →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/digitaldemocracy2030/kouchou-ai"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <hgroup class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <div class="gradient w-1"></div>
        <div class="w-[calc(100%-12px)]">
          <h3 class="text-2xl">Idobata</h3>
          <p class="font-bold mt-2">
            A platform for large-scale deliberation and policy feedback.
          </p>
        </div>
      </hgroup>
      <img
        src="/en/images/idobata-diagram.webp"
        width="1672"
        height="941"
        alt="Idobata image"
        class="w-full mt-4"
      />
      <p class="mt-4">
        Inspired by Taiwan&apos;s vTaiwan and JOIN platforms, Idobata supports
        online deliberation by helping participants express views, identify
        important issues, discuss possible responses, and move from public input
        toward better decisions.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/idobata/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-primary">
          Learn more (Japanese) →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/digitaldemocracy2030/idobata"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <hgroup class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <div class="gradient w-1"></div>
        <div class="w-[calc(100%-12px)]">
          <h3 class="text-2xl">Polimoney</h3>
          <p class="font-bold mt-2">
            Political finance transparency through open data and visualization.
          </p>
        </div>
      </hgroup>
      <img
        src="/en/images/polimoney-dashboard.webp"
        width="1697"
        height="927"
        alt="Polimoney dashboard image"
        class="w-full mt-4 py-2"
      />
      <p class="mt-4">
        Inspired in part by Sweden&apos;s transparent political-finance practices,
        Polimoney makes political finance information easier to see and discuss.
        The goal is to reduce opacity around political money and make public
        accounting more understandable.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/polimoney/" hreflang="ja" class="btn btn-primary">
          Learn more (Japanese) →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://polimoney.dd2030.org/"
          hreflang="ja"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Website (Japanese) →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/digitaldemocracy2030/polimoney"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <hgroup class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <div class="gradient w-1"></div>
        <div class="w-[calc(100%-12px)]">
          <h3 class="text-2xl">Project Coreloop</h3>
          <p class="font-bold mt-2">
            From listening to agreement, policy, execution, and feedback.
          </p>
        </div>
      </hgroup>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Project Coreloop explores how public input can move beyond collection
        into consensus-building, policy design, implementation, and visible
        social improvement.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a
          href="https://coreloop.dd2030.org/"
          class="btn btn-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Learn more →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://antifraud.dd2030.org/"
          hreflang="ja"
          class="btn btn-outline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Anti-fraud project (Japanese) →
